  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Development Alliance (GDA) with Pamir Energy (PE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tajikistan):  .The GDA with Pamir Energy will increase access to electricity for the residents of the remote village of Murghab in eastern Tajikistan to affordable, reliable, and clean energy by adding 800-kilowatt (kw) of additional capacity to an existing off-grid 200 kw solar PV station. The activity will integrate sustainable utility-based electrification strategies with renewable energy solutions that decrease reliance on carbon-emitting biofuels, build strategies to equip communities with and develop climate change resilience, and lay the foundation for catalytic socio-economic development.  This activity contributes $1 million of the Mission&apos;s $1 million Renewable Energy earmark...This activity will promote Tajikistan&apos;s broad-based economic prosperity, and human development to promote competitiveness, energy and water security, and improved livelihoods, which contributes to ICS goal 3. It supports the CAS objectives by promoting private sector led growth and supporting energy independence..</narrative>
  </description>
